in a last-ditch election effort green  party candidate annalena berbock tries  to convince voters that she is best  suited to become germany's leader  targeting mainly young people like lucas  weidinger who feel disgruntled by the  status quo and are calling for change i  had some contacts with  the classical more classical older  parties and i i was a little bit  disappointed because i thought like  that that's not how i want to play  politics right and that's not i don't  feel that i really can make a difference  i can only participate in continuing the  same same thing over and over  climate change social justice and  equality are among top concerns for a  generation that grew up in the air of  globalization and the internet the youth  represent less than 15 percent of the  electorate and among them first-time  voters who have known no other leader  than angela merkel but they are trying  to have an impact on the outcome of the  election  they are the so-called miracle  generation one that mostly thinks the  outgoing chancellor wasn't progressive  enough  and they've grown more demanding  maintaining pressure on the streets with  climate protest groups like the friday  for future movement  this is also their last ditch attempt to  make their voices heard less than 48  hours ahead of what rifke lambrecht  calls a historic election  she has put her future on hold saying  there are more pressing issues to be  dealt with first exactly because our  future is in big danger actually if we  are not putting our  studies on hold for example now to go on  the streets to protest  to try our best to change something then  my studies probably won't help me in 50  years anymore because we will have  floods and  war and lots of refugees so the 60-plus  people will decide about our future  so it's so important to convince the old  generation to vote for the young  generation somehow  this has pushed politicians to listen  and address the concerns of young people  says vasily goload he is the co-host of  machiavelli a popular podcast that links  rap and politics  some of the candidates took part in his  show including center left social  democrat leader olaf schultz they need  the young people because they see that  older people also start to think about  the following generations there is  pressure there is pressure from the  streets there is pressure from the young  generation on the streets there is  pressure from young journalists there is  pressure from  musicians so i think in in the whole  society we see that there is a shift  there is a change and  probably we will also see this change  after the election in many ways angela  merkel has shaped german youth they are  a minority of voters but in this tight  race could emerge crucial to whoever  reaches the finishing line first  abdel hamid al-jazeera cologne germany
 

